1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Andrew Sinclair (privy counsellor)=
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Andrew_Sinclair_(privy_counsellor '''Sir Andrew Sinclair of Ravenscraig'''], in Denmark known as Anders Sincklar (Sinklar, Sinclar), til Ravenscraig og [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sinclairsholm_Ca
2 CONC stle Sincklarsholm], born 1555, died 1625, was a Scotsman of noble birth, who became a Danish privy counsellor, envoy to England, colonel, and holder of extensive fiefs.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Early life===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sinclair was the third''' son of Henry, fifth [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lord_Sinclair Lord Sinclair], and Janet Lindsay, in his fathers first marriage. For a period he was brought up at the court of [https://en.wikipedia.o
2 CONC rg/wiki/Henry_I,_Duke_of_Guise Henry I, Duke of Guise]. It is assumed that Sinclair came to Denmark in connection with the marriage between [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/James_VI_and_I King James VI] and [https://en.wikipedia.org
2 CONC /wiki/Anne_of_Denmark Anne of Denmark]. He became [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Valet_de_chambre hofjunker] to [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Christian_IV_of_Denmark Christian IV of Denmark] in 1591, and in 1597 [https://en.wikip
2 CONC edia.org/wiki/Groom_of_the_Chamber kammerjunker] to the queen, [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anne_Catherine_of_Brandenburg Anne Catherine of Brandenburg]. After his marriage 1600, Sinclair left the court, and became a fief-holder
2 CONC  in Skåne. Sinclair fought in the Kalmar war as captain of a company of the King's regiment of foot, and participated in the Danish capture of Öland. After the Danish capture of Kalmar he became military governor of the city.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Political role===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''In 1606 Sinclair was''' involved in correspondence with [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lady_Arbella_Stuart Arbella Stuart] and [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Margaret_Howard,_Countess_of_Nottingham Margaret Howard, Countess of 
2 CONC Nottingham] when the Countess accused Christian IV of insulting her. Sinclair wrote to Arbella that Christian hoped she might defend his honour.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Christian IV aggressive''' policy towards Sweden was met with reluctance and skepticism in Skåne, since the province would be the first to feel the impact of war in case of hostilities. The King needed faithful supporters in th
2 CONC e province, and hence Sinclair was made colonel of the Scanian Regiment in 1615, and became recipient of a number of land donations. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''The following year he''' was made one of a very limited number of knights of the Order of the Armed Arm. In 1617 Sinclair became a member of the privy council of the Danish realm; the King needed loyal followers in that august 
2 CONC body, as its resistance towards his foreign policy was mounting. He was the King's confidential adviser in matters concerning Great Britain, utilizing his many friends and connections to Danish advantage, especially James VI, with
2 CONC  whom he was in great favour. Sinclair was the Danish King's envoy in Britain a number of times between 1606 and 1621, managing to influence James VI into adopting a more pro-Danish, and less pro-Swedish, stance. At the same time 
2 CONC Sinclair acted as the British King's emissary at the Danish court.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Personal life===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''In 1600, Sinclair married''' Kirsten Eriksdatter Kaas, in a ceremony at the Royal Palace. She was maid of honour to the Queen, and of the Danish noble family af Sparre. They had three sons, and one daughter; Jakob (James) Sincl
2 CONC air (who also served James VI), Johanne Andersdatter Sinclair, Erik Sinclair, and Christian Sinclair. Sinclair had [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gladsaxehus Gladsaxehus] as a fief, 1600–1620; Gislöv from 1613; Landskrona 1619–162
2 CONC 1, then exchanged against [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hammershus Hammershus]. The King gave him Sandby in Göinge as allodial possession; in the vicinity he began to build Sinclairsholm, which, however, was not completed until a
2 CONC fter his death. He also held [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kronovall_Castle Kronovall] until his death.<br/>
2 CONT <br/>
